ases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]ref_create_force_recapture.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/ref_create_force_recapture.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-c9[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-c9/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reading families in the library read model[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]family[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]family: teach ref_library the note-local earlier: list, reading numbers,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and families. Doctor stops flagging families as duplicate_identity, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]find/show/resolve rank the newest reading first, list/show render vN [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]chips and earlier/later rows, and JSON grows additively; uses [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hand-written fixtures only.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One already-captured refusal, before parent resolution[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]refusal[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refusal: route every duplicate site (URL dedupe, same-reference stem [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]walk, library PDF as TARGET, collections) through one renderer that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lists every copy and prints several hint rows. Duplicate detection runs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]before the missing -P error. -f semantics are unchanged.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The --force[=MODE] parser and bare -f reread[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]reread[dim] · [dim][/dim]after family, refusal[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reread: turn -f into --force[=MODE], with adjacent-mode adoption and a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stray-mode guard, and replace the bool with Option<ForceMode>. Ship [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reread end to end: the <root>__vN allocator, earlier: written at birth [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](inline and queued), the -vN block-id suffix, the 'Title (vN)' alias, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]-P/-t defaults from the family, hints, refusals, the reread: output [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]line, collections with an exact URL set, docs. overwrite parses but [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]refuses until the next phase.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]In-place overwrite of unannotated references[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]overwrite[dim] · [dim][/dim]after reread[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]overwrite: -f overwrite on any host, for references with no PDF [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]annotations. Includes rename-style preconditions, -N member selection, a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]render-first locked transaction with a host-local intent marker and HEAD[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rollback, sidecar removal, and a frozen inert note in ref_history/ when [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]there is authored prose. Also earlier: carry-forward, recaptured:, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]success output, the overwrite refusal hints, and docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Annotated overwrite on the Mac[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]annotated[dim] · [dim][/dim]after overwrite[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]annotated: overwrite references that carry highlights, image selections,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]or .assets/, on macOS only and only under [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]highlights.coordinate_pdf_writes. Rename the annotated PDF and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]assets into ref_history/, move inbound #^h- links to the frozen note, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add the scan write-back guard, extend the acceptance runbook, and refuse[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with a hint on other hosts.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Decision record, glossary correction, and final docs pass[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]record[dim] · [dim][/dim]after annotated[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]record: write the accepted recapture decision record and correct the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Reference Task glossary strand, then republish memory. Run the final [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cross-page docs consistency pass and docs-check, and record proposed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]follow-ups.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-c9","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-c9.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-c95947bf6fcefe9de1455435bda52e10","started_at":"2026-10-25T18:18:18.134999+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[{"committed_at":1792965180,"sha":"291efa6b374695cace353fab593504d5c0cc6600","subject":"feat(highlights): derive birth earlier lineage and reading-aware ref task IDs"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"8cd0d1e8d45ee3223c9b2653d95db5b23f04b9d3ee0a5da384703b3e4e0d052d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-c9.3.1.3/chat.md","size_bytes":4578},"commits":{"digest":"00443331655ecf517eb05b343e3db613ecc9dfc25895f737159463609599007b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-c9.3.1.3/commits.json","size_bytes":255},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"3942241a63c5de53df93bede886ed35a51f8b6a33d5883d819c898d7dd34f408","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-c9.3.1.3/emb